Title: THE INTERROGATION
Author: ActorRoom Studio

INT. POLICE INTERROGATION ROOM - NIGHT

The harsh incandescent bulb hums above a scarred metal table. DETECTIVE MILLER leans forward, eyes piercing. Across from him sits VIKTOR, hands cuffed.

DETECTIVE MILLER
(leaning in, voice low)
Sit down, Viktor. We both know how this ends.

VIKTOR
(smiling faintly)
Do we, Detective? Because from where I'm sitting, your case fell apart an hour ago.

DETECTIVE MILLER
(slamming folder on table)
We found the ledger at the docks. Your signature. Your shell company.

VIKTOR
(unfazed)
A forgery. Cheap ink, careless handwriting. You’re grasping at shadows, Miller.

DETECTIVE MILLER
(sharp)
Where were you on the night of the fourteenth?

VIKTOR
(deadpan)
Ask your chief. I was having dinner with him.
